cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cairn, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cairn: An Adaptable Framework for Scientist-AI Research Software Teams"
abstract: >-
  Cairn is a methodology for scientist-led research-software teams
  adopting AI agents: an invariant doctrine of recorded, reviewed
  deliberation; forkable templates; a single-agent bootstrap that
  adapts the apparatus along codebase and team dimensions; and two
  worked case studies (modflow_tools and LHM).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kendall
    given-names: Anthony
    affiliation: "Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences, Michigan State University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9964"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-06-12"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MSUHydrogeology/cairn-scientist-ai-teams"
license:
